# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Flutter Chat App — environment variable reference
# Copy this file to .env (never commit .env)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── LLM provider (OpenAI-compatible) ─────────────────────────────
# Defaults target Google Gemini, which has a generous free tier.
# Get a free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
LLM_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

# Optional — override the default model
# The Gemini OpenAI-compatibility endpoint expects the `models/` prefix.
# LLM_MODEL=models/gemini-3.6-flash

# Optional — override the endpoint to switch providers.
# Gemini (default):
#   LLM_API_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/chat/completions
# Groq:
#   LLM_API_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions
#   LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
# OpenAI:
#   LLM_API_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions
#   LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW THE API KEY IS USED
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Option A — Flutter client (development / quick start)
#   Pass at build time so the app calls the LLM directly:
#     flutter run --dart-define=LLM_API_KEY=$LLM_API_KEY
#     flutter build apk --dart-define=LLM_API_KEY=$LLM_API_KEY
#
#   ⚠ The key is embedded in the compiled binary. Fine for personal
#     dev use; NOT suitable for public apps.
#
# Option B — Firebase Cloud Function (recommended for production)
#   Store the key as a Firebase secret — it never leaves the server:
#     firebase functions:secrets:set GROQ_API_KEY
#   Then deploy the function (requires the Blaze plan):
#     cd functions && npm install && firebase deploy --only functions
#   The Flutter app writes user messages to Firestore; the function
#   reacts, calls the LLM, and writes the reply back automatically.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
